      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we need to know the initial day of the week (November 23) and then calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23 and find the corresponding day of the week.\n\n1. Identify the initial day of the week:\n   - November 23 is given as Thursday.\n\n2. Calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23:\n   - The number of days in November from November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n   - The number of days in December from December 1 to December 23 is \\(23 - 1 + 1 = 23\\) days.\n   - Therefore, the total number of days between November 23 and December 23 is \\(8 + 23 = 31\\) days.\n\n3. Determine the day of the week after \\(31\\) days from Thursday:\n   - Since there are 7 days in a week, we can find the equivalent day by calculating the remainder of \\(31\\) divided by \\(7\\):\n     \\[\n     31 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ R } 3\n     \\]\n   - This means \\(31\\) days is equivalent to \\(4\\) weeks and \\(3\\) days. Starting from Thursday, adding 3 days brings us to:\n     - Week 1: Thursday + 1 day = Friday\n     - Week 2: Friday + 1 day = Saturday\n     - Week 3: Saturday + 1 day = Sunday\n   - Therefore, December 23 is a Sunday.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
